flowchart LR
    %% "attempt" counts marks of the current item across every branch; MAX = 2.
    %% Speaker: marked PASS -> professor, marked FAIL -> student.

    A[TA marks Pass / Fail] --> REV{Correct status already told?}

    %% ===== AFTER THE REVEAL =====
    REV -->|Yes| RB{Correct status?}
    RB -->|Yes| RC[Speaker: That's it — thanks]
    RC --> R[Item resolved]
    RB -->|No| RD[Speaker: It should be X — re-mark it]
    RD --> A

    %% ===== EVERY OTHER MARK =====
    REV -->|No| CH{Correct PASS?}
    CH -->|Yes, 80%| R
    CH -->|Otherwise| T[Lock pass/fail buttons]
    T --> U[Speaker asks: Are you sure this is a PASS/FAIL?]
    U --> V{TA response — LLM classifies}

    V -->|Unclear, 1st time| CL[Speaker: Just to check — are you keeping it as PASS/FAIL?]
    CL --> V
    V -->|Unclear, 2nd time| NO

    V -->|Yes| B{Correct status?}
    B -->|Yes| K[Speaker gives brief affirmation + why the step meets / misses the criterion]
    K --> R

    B -->|No| AB[Speaker asks: Why does this step meet / miss the criterion?]
    AB --> AC[TA explains]
    AC --> AD[Speaker: Consider this: what the criterion checks, pointing at the step]
    AD --> AE[TA responds]
    AE --> AT

    V -->|No| NO{Correct status?}
    NO -->|Yes| M[Speaker asks: What about the call are you unsure about?]
    NO -->|No| W[Speaker asks: Then what do you think is off, and why?]
    M --> N[TA responds]
    W --> N
    N --> AT

    %% ===== SHARED ATTEMPT CHECK =====
    AT{Attempt < 2?}
    AT -->|Yes| Z[Speaker: Take another look and mark it the way you think is right<br/>Unlock buttons]
    Z --> A
    AT -->|No| AA[Speaker tells the correct status + explanation<br/>Unlock — TA must re-mark it]
    AA --> A

    R --> NEXT[Next criterion]
